and power generation applications; prefabricated and site-built residential homes, flooring products; insulation, roofing, and engineered products; building and engineered components; paints and coatings; and bricks and masonry products, as well as offers manufactured and site-built home construction, and related lending and financial services. In addition, the company provides recreational vehicles, apparel, footwear, toys, jewelry, custom picture framing products, alkaline batteries, logistics services, and professional aviation training and shared aircraft ownership programs; castings, forgings, fasteners/fastener systems, aerostructures, and precision components; and cobalt, nickel, and titanium alloys. Further, it distributes televisions and information, and grocery and non-food consumer products; franchises and services quick service restaurants; and distributes electronic components. Additionally, it retails automobiles; furniture, bedding, and accessories; household appliances, electronics, and floor coverings; watches, home decor and repair services; sells kitchenware; and motorcycle clothing and equipment. The company was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Omaha, Nebraska.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gregory Edward Abel | CEO, President & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $22.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 387K people. Revenue per employee of $958K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $65K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 23\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Berkshire Hathaway Inc. New is a mega-cap financial services business with a $1.2T market cap on $371.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $25.0B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.69\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 98% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9787391415203549},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 119% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (96% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $533.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why JPMorgan Chase Fans May Look To ETFs Right Now","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/options/articles/why-jpmorgan-chase-fans-may-211349086.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795814029.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Do 3 ETFs Change Your JPMorgan Chase Risk?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/etfs/us/nysearca-mgv/news/how-do-3-etfs-change-your-jpmorgan-chase-risk","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795813911.793,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Warren's wisdom: How would Buffett invest with high inflation?","source":"fool.com.au","link":"https://www.fool.com.au/2026/11/28/warrens-wisdom-how-would-buffett-invest-with-high-inflation/","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795813200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Berkshire Hathaway (BRK.A) Takes $930 Million Equity Stake In A Private Tech Company","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/berkshire-hathaway-brk-takes-930-200838928.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795810118.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Caterpillar is quietly 